        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whey is the more efficient protein: more leucine per gram, higher digestibility, smoother texture, lower heavy-metal levels on average and usually a lower cost per 25 g. Plant protein closes most of that gap the moment you dose it properly, at roughly 30-35 g per serving, and the long-term training studies show similar muscle and strength gains when total protein is adequate.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you digest dairy, whey is the default, and an isolate fixes most lactose problems. If you are vegan, have a milk allergy or simply prefer plants, choose a pea, soy or multi-source blend, take a slightly bigger scoop and buy a third-party tested product. Either way, your daily protein total matters far more than which tub it came from.
